# @epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_well_formed — the
# DECLARATIVE HALF of bilateral pattern #53's FOURTH INSTANCE at
# supervision altitude. Substrate-pull-correct property asserting:
# a `restart_intensity` carrier is well-formed at declaration time
# — non-degenerate budget, non-zero period, ratio within the
# supervision-altitude sane range.
#
# Closes the bilateral pair forward-promised by
# `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror` lines 269-272 (Seam audit
# `f732d9c` §Next-/loop) and pairs with the operational half at
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm` (sibling shard, same tick).
#
# === The bilateral pattern (#53; fourth instance) ===
#
# First instance:  keyword/depth
#                  (@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth +
#                   @kintsugi/fracture/keyword; 2026-06-10
#                   `5e68df9` + `d908798`; per-predicate).
# Second instance: gate/diff-closure
#                  (@epistemologic/pact/gate_matches_diff_closure +
#                   @kintsugi/fracture/gate; 2026-06-16;
#                   per-predicate; promotion tick for #53).
# Third instance:  syntax-substrate-native / angle_to_paren
#                  (@epistemologic/pact/syntax_substrate_native +
#                   @kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren; 2026-06-19;
#                   parametric-over-table).
# Third instance also: symbol/canonical-form / symbol_lift +
#                  operator/composition-primitive / operator_match
#                  (parametric-over-table variants).
# Fourth instance (THIS): restart_intensity_well_formed +
#                  @kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm at SUPERVISION
#                  altitude. The pattern absorbs the supervision-
#                  altitude carrier variant — the property predicates
#                  over a typed record (not a source token) whose
#                  well-formedness gates a runtime kintsugi loop.
#                  Substrate vocabulary unchanged; same @glass
#                  opacity + @kintsugi/consent morphism chain.
#
# === The predicate ===
#
# Given the landed `restart_intensity` carrier (Mara `a3dcb94`,
# `shards/spectral/restart_intensity.mirror`):
#
#   type restart_intensity = {
#     budget: ref,      # initial B₀; monotone descent per @loop
#     period: duration, # time window within which budget applies
#   }
#
# `well_formed(ri: restart_intensity) -> verdict` reduces to a
# three-conjunct at supervision altitude:
#
#   well_formed(ri) ⇔
#       budget_positive(ri.budget)
#     ∧ period_positive(ri.period)
#     ∧ ratio_within_supervision_range(ri.budget, ri.period)
#
# Conjunct rationale, per emergent-supervision `a3dec7b` §5.5's
# H4 discussion:
#
# - `budget_positive`: B₀ = 0 is a DEGENERATE storm-protector —
#   the supervisor escalates on the FIRST failure, indistinguishable
#   from having no restart intensity at all (and worse than absent:
#   the field's presence suggests the supervisor considered storm
#   protection). Substrate-pull-correct: forbid the degenerate
#   declaration; the empty-configuration path is `option::none`
#   on `restart_intensity`, not a zero-budget declaration.
#
# - `period_positive`: A zero-duration window is degenerate for the
#   same structural reason — any single restart consumes the whole
#   budget in a zero-width window; the ratio (§5.3 step 4) becomes
#   `budget / 0`. Undefined. Substrate-pull-correct: the period IS
#   the substrate-time predicate over the loop's tick_history; a
#   zero-width window carries no predicate content.
#
# - `ratio_within_supervision_range`: Per emergent-supervision §5.5
#   the (budget, period) ratio names how aggressive the storm
#   detector is. BEAM defaults (max_restarts = 3, max_seconds = 5)
#   sit at 3/5 = 0.6 restarts/second at supervision altitude. The
#   sane range this conjunct guards: `budget / period.seconds ≤
#   ratio_ceiling` where `ratio_ceiling` names the substrate's
#   default (initial ceiling 10 restarts/second — one order of
#   magnitude above BEAM's default, wide enough to accommodate
#   fast-boot children while still catching pathological
#   deterministic-failure storms). The ceiling is substrate-decl-
#   configurable per-supervisor; this predicate reads the ceiling
#   from the supervisor's substrate context.
#
# The three-conjunct guards against the three degenerate declaration
# shapes: zero-budget (silent no-op), zero-period (undefined ratio),
# and pathological-ratio (permits arbitrarily fast storm — defeats
# the purpose of the field). Any violation surfaces one opacity
# per offending field, which the paired fracture body reads.
#
# === Composes with @spawn ≤ @loop ===
#
# Per emergent-supervision §5.3: the restart intensity IS a
# `@spawn ≤ @loop` at supervision altitude. Each restart is one
# `bind` step; the budget's monotone descent IS the halting witness.
# This property's `well_formed` verdict gates whether the loop
# instantiation is admissible at declaration time — before any
# child spawns, the supervisor's restart intensity must be
# well-formed; else the storm-protector's contract is broken
# at the source, and the fracture body surfaces the malformation
# through the paired `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm` at
# realisation time.
#
# The property fires at declaration time (compile-time gate); the
# paired fracture fires at runtime AT MOST when the (well-formed)
# intensity's budget is empirically exhausted (§5.5's H4 empirical
# validation flag — DEFERRED per this cascade's discipline).
#
# === Rice-safety ===
#
# Per emergent-supervision §5.4: the supervisor cannot ask "will
# this peer eventually stop failing?" (Rice forbids it). This
# property asks the DECIDABLE question: "is the declaration well-
# formed at supervision altitude?" — a syntactic three-conjunct on
# a landed carrier's fields. Substrate-pull-correct scope: the
# witness is the carrier, not the peer's future behaviour.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   BEAM `max_restarts / max_seconds` validation
#                              Armstrong (1996) *Making reliable
#                              distributed systems in the presence
#                              of software errors*, PhD thesis
#                              Ch. 4 §4.3.3. OTP's `supervisor`
#                              behaviour rejects `max_restarts < 0`
#                              at `init/1` return time; this property
#                              lifts the discipline to substrate-decl
#                              altitude and adds the positive-period
#                              + ratio-ceiling conjuncts.
#   Floyd-Hoare precondition   Floyd (1967) *Assigning meanings to
#                              programs* + Hoare (1969) *An
#                              axiomatic basis for computer
#                              programming*. Well-formedness IS the
#                              declaration-time precondition over
#                              the (budget, period) pair; the
#                              supervisor's storm-protection contract
#                              is a Hoare triple whose precondition
#                              this property discharges.
#   ranking function ceiling   Termination proofs via well-founded
#                              orders; the ratio ceiling names the
#                              supervision-altitude well-founded
#                              base. Per emergent-supervision §5.4
#                              "escalation by monotone descent" is
#                              well-founded ONLY when the initial
#                              rate is bounded away from ∞.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
# - `ratio_ceiling` is per-supervisor substrate-decl-configurable.
#   The initial default (10 restarts/second) is an operational
#   choice, not a substrate-mathematical one. Different supervision
#   subtrees may declare tighter or looser ceilings via the
#   supervisor's substrate context. This property reads the ceiling
#   from context; it does NOT hardcode a substrate-wide value.
#
# - The ratio conjunct assumes `period.nanos > 0` — the ordering
#   `budget_positive ∧ period_positive` before
#   `ratio_within_supervision_range` is load-bearing.
#
# - Whether these three conjuncts are EMPIRICALLY sufficient to
#   catch every degenerate declaration is DEFERRED per
#   [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]]. The
#   analytical shape is right; the empirical audit lands when a
#   runtime supervisor exercises a live restart-intensity storm.
#   Seam audit `f732d9c` and emergent-supervision §5.5 H4 both
#   flag the same DEFER.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/supervisor/emergent-supervision-from-
#               geometry.md §5.5 (Mara `a3dec7b`; the math floor
#               for the (budget, period) ratio discussion and
#               the empirical H4 flag),
#               docs/audits/2026-07-03-seam-restart-intensity-
#               shard.md (Seam audit `f732d9c` naming this
#               bilateral pair as the next-/loop tick),
#               shards/spectral/restart_intensity.mirror (Mara
#               `a3dcb94`; the CARRIER this property predicates
#               on),
#               shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror (the
#               forward-promise at lines 269-272 this landing
#               closes),
#               docs/math/kintsugi/compiler-error-surface.md §1
#               + `9f4211d` (the three-mode algebra the paired
#               fracture body's morphism proposes over).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53; this is the fourth instance),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (@epistemologic = form-side family root;
#                       this property sits form-side; the paired
#                       fracture at @kintsugi sits process-side),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                       property's decidability rests on the landed
#                       `duration` carrier; no bare integers cross
#                       the predicate boundary),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] + [[feedback-
#                       explicit-over-implicit]] (`restart_intensity`,
#                       `verdict`, and the sub-predicates are all
#                       typed carriers; no primitive-over-primitive
#                       comparisons at the substrate boundary),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (grep 2026-07-03 confirmed no `restart_storm`
#                       or `well_formed`-on-supervision-carrier
#                       precedent; `well_formed` exists at other
#                       altitudes as expected bilateral pattern).
# Related shards: spectral/restart_intensity.mirror (the carrier
#                  this property predicates on; landed `a3dcb94`),
#                 spectral/supervisor.mirror (the supervision-
#                  altitude family root under which the carrier
#                  lives),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.mirror (the
#                  OPERATIONAL HALF of this bilateral pair; sibling
#                  shard in this same tick),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/angle_to_paren.mirror (the third
#                  instance whose fracture-body shape this bilateral
#                  follows — same opacity → morphism arrow;
#                  supervision-altitude specialisation of the
#                  syntax-altitude precedent),
#                 epistemologic/property/dark_count_monotone.mirror
#                  (sibling in @epistemologic/property; monotone
#                  witness at a different substrate altitude;
#                  vocabulary parallel).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_well_formed.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_well_formed`
