source @arxiv/programming/floyd-hoare-1969
source @arxiv/beam/armstrong-thesis-1996

# === well_formed predicate (declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that the
# restart_intensity is well-formed at supervision altitude — its
# budget is positive, its period is positive, and their ratio is
# within the substrate's per-supervisor sane range.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the @kintsugi loop's
# active_pass reads this predicate during the supervisor's
# declaration-time gate. The operational half (the fracture body
# that emits a widen/raise/surface morphism when this predicate
# fails) lives at `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm` (sibling shard
# in this same tick).
#
# Verdict semantics:
#   success            — all three conjuncts hold; declaration is
#                        well-formed; the supervisor's storm-
#                        protection contract is admissible.
#   failure(opacity_map)
#                      — at least one conjunct fails; the opacity_map
#                        names the offending field(s). The paired
#                        fracture body reads one opacity at a time
#                        and emits a morphism per site (widen the
#                        period, raise the budget, or surface as
#                        Tomm question per compiler-error-surface
#                        §8's three-mode algebra when the
#                        malformation is out-of-band-resolvable).
well_formed(ri: restart_intensity) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/restart_intensity_well_formed
out well_formed
